{"d.Log is passed instead of the operation-scoped log variable that includes context fields (name, kind, method), losing diagnostic information in downstream logs and async context for legacy writes": 0.9446946382522583, "recordLegacyDuration is called when unified Storage.Create fails, but should be recordStorageDuration instead - this misattributes storage failures to legacy operations in metrics, skewing migration readiness dashboards and SLO calculations": 0.9840342998504639, "name (object name) is passed as a metric label where other methods use options.Kind for resource kind - this introduces high cardinality and breaks metric consistency across operations": 0.9402686953544617, "Inside the async legacy DeleteCollection goroutine, recordStorageDuration is called instead of recordLegacyDuration - this mislabels legacy async operation metrics": 0.9958788156509399, "Async legacy writes lack any logging on failure\u2014only metrics\u2014which breaks visibility into divergence between unified and legacy storage during rollback scenarios": 0.9268772602081299, "Unbounded goroutine spawning under high write load or slow legacy backends creates resource leak risk": 0.6761433482170105, "Hardcoded 10-second timeout is not tunable across environments": 0.24801765382289886, "No backpressure or queue depth visibility exists for async operations": 0.1682940274477005, "Unit tests don't validate async behavior completes": 0.47868043184280396, "Integration tests don't verify cross-store consistency or dual-write metrics": 0.15562069416046143, "No timeout or goroutine lifecycle scenarios are tested": 0.29380837082862854}